"moments": [
{"title": "Chasing the light", "text": "You leave before sunrise to be in position as the first light spills across the plains. Mist hangs low over the grass, and a line of zebras walks through it in silhouette. Your guide stops at just the right angle. The shutter clicks, and the day has already rewarded you."},
{"title": "The long wait", "text": "A pair of cheetahs rests on a mound, eyes half closed. Your guide switches off the engine, and you settle in. Twenty minutes pass, then forty. You watch the light shift, adjust your settings, and wait. Patience is part of the craft, and the bush rarely hurries."},
{"title": "The decisive moment", "text": "Then a head lifts, ears forward. The cheetahs rise and stretch, and suddenly everything aligns: the light, the background, the gesture. You shoot steadily, breath held, knowing this is the frame you came for. It lasts seconds, but it was worth every minute of waiting."},
{"title": "Reviewing the day", "text": "Back at camp, you scroll through the day's images with a drink in hand. Some are near misses, some surprise you, and one or two make you smile. Your guide asks to see the best shot. Tomorrow, you agree, you will try that angle again."}
],
